From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0327: the test tones are quiet

0194 made the ADSP beep tone near full scale (-1 dBFS) because the
bring-up had nothing to compare it to, and the buffers it rings are also
what kern.sweet_audio op 1 replays. iOS's volume never reaches it:
stream_volume() only moves the RX macro gains when iOS's own stream
starts, so a beep plays at 0 dB whatever the phone's volume says. The
tone is -31 dBFS now: still easy to find by ear on the headphones, no
longer alarming. (userland/audio/tone_test.c drops its 440 Hz tone to
-38 dBFS to match; that one does go through the volume.)
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
index 05e5e57..70217d4 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
@@ -12388,10 +12388,10 @@ audio_test(void)
 	IOSleep(300);
 	/* kept for the rest of the session: the ADSP may hold on to the mapping */
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < A_NBUF * A_PERIOD; i++) {
-		/* 1 kHz at 48 kHz: 48 samples a period; a triangle near full scale (the buffers alternate tone / silence below) */
+		/* 1 kHz at 48 kHz: 48 samples a period; a quiet triangle (the buffers alternate tone / silence below) */
 		int ph = (int)(i % 48);
 		int tri = ph < 24 ? ph * 2 - 24 : 72 - ph * 2;   /* -24..24 */
-		buf[i] = (int16_t)(tri * 1200);
+		buf[i] = (int16_t)(tri * 40);       /* 0327: -31 dBFS: loud at 0 dB RX gain, and iOS's volume does not reach it */
 	}
 	bzero(buf + 4 * A_PERIOD, 4 * A_PERIOD * sizeof(int16_t));   /* buffers 4-7 silent: beeps */
 	mb();
